I fixed #1028: a bad max_tokens, temperature, max_turns or context_window value in .yoyo.toml now prints a warning on stderr instead of being dropped silently. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the format check pass, and it's committed as 32e13379.

Change
• The parsing now lives in a new function, cli_config::resolve_numeric_setting. It returns the value plus any warning text, so the tests check the exact string a user sees. parse_numeric_flag in src/cli.rs just prints those warnings, in the same style and on the same channel as the existing flag warning.
• Example: `warning: Invalid max_tokens value 'abc' in config file, using default`. Nothing else changes: the default is still used, the exit code is still 0, and a flag still overrides the config.
• The config value is cleaned with sanitize_for_display before printing, since it comes from the repository.
• **One choice to know about:** if a valid flag overrides a bad config value, the bad value gets no warning. That run never uses it, so "using default" would be false. If the flag is also invalid, both warn. A test pins this.
• I didn't reuse validate_config_value. Its range rules differ from what runtime actually does (it rejects temperature above 2.0, while runtime clamps above 1.0), and it has no context_window rule. It's also the one the issue suggested, so the commit says why.

Checks
• I built the release binary and ran it in a temp repo once per bad line: "abc", -5 and 99999999999 for max_tokens, temperature = "hot", max_turns = "x" and context_window = "big". Each printed exactly one warning, still answered PONG and exited 0. A valid line (max_tokens = 2048) printed nothing.
• New tests cover a bad value for each key, valid values staying silent and unchanged, the flag-override choice, and an escape character in the value. When I removed the warning temporarily, exactly the three failure tests failed by name; I put it back and everything passed. The existing test test_parse_numeric_flag_invalid_config_returns_none passes without edits.
• `src/cli.rs` got 7 lines shorter, so I lowered its entry in the file-size check to 7685.
• `docs/src/getting-started/installation.md` now says a bad value warns and falls back to the default.

Same problem elsewhere, filed as #1030: two more settings drop a bad value silently, and the issue doesn't cover them, so the commit can still say Fixes #1028. I confirmed both on the binary:
• `max_auto_continues` in the config is dropped without a word.
• `cost_warn_usd, --cost-warn and YOYO_COST_WARN_USD` are worse: a mistyped spending limit turns the limit off, with no warning from any of the three.
